</div>
<div align="left"> <br />
<p align="center">&nbsp; <font color="#ff0000"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt" size="4"><strong>September 4,
2007</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="4"><strong>HUMOR</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">A muddy-wet priest and pastor from two
local churches are standing by the side of the road, frantically pounding a
sign into the ground that reads,</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">The End is
Near!</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Turn yourself around
now!</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Before it's too
late!</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">&quot;Leave us alone you fanatics!&quot;
yelled a driver as he sped by.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">From around the curve came the sound of
screeching tires and a big splash.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">The pastor turns to the priest and says,
&quot;I told you this sign should just say 'Bridge
Out'?&quot;</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">.....</font></font><font color="#000000"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"> Notes from your Chaplain -
</font></font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">Chap
Notes (</font></font><font color="#0000ff"><u><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2">http://www.chapnotes.org)
(</font></font></u></font><font color="#0000ff"><u><a
href="mailto:ChapNotesMail@aol.com"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">ChapNotesMail@aol.com</font></font></a></u></font><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">) by way of &ldquo;Christian
Voices&rdquo;</font></font><font color="#0000ff"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"> (</font></font></font><font
color="#0000ff"><u><a href="http://www.christianvoicesworldwide.com/"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">www.ChristianVoicesWorldwide.com</font></font></a></u></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>THOUGHT PROVOKING &ndash;
INSPIRATIONAL</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><strong><font face="Arial,
sans-serif">THERE IS NO &quot;FUN&quot; IN
DYSFUNCTIONAL</font></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">What child doesn't like
to imitate his parents? Little girls put on mommy's lipstick and little
boys clomp around in daddy's shoes. Unfortunately, we often imitate bad
habits of our parents too. Sometimes parents model negative behaviors that
can ruin our lives if we imitate them. Addictions and abuse are behaviors
that we would be better off not copying.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">That's what
dysfunctional families are all about -- kids copying their parents -- and
hurting themselves and others as a result. </font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">We often find ourselves
demonstrating behaviors we dislike. For some reason, it&rsquo;s much easier
to pick up another&rsquo;s bad habits than it is to learn their good
habits. Once ingrained, negative traits and habits become like chains that
are nearly impossible to break, but here's some good news: God says,
&quot;You were redeemed from the empty way of life handed down to you from
your forefathers.&quot; (I Peter 1:18-19) In other words, there's hope of
changing and ridding your life of some of those &quot;empty ways&quot; you
learned while growing up.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">The dark stuff inside us
- whether it's from our past or from our own choices - is wrapped up in
what God calls &quot;sin.&quot; Sin, simply put, is living in a way
that&rsquo;s not good for us or those around us. It&rsquo;s falling short
of the best God has planned for us. </font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Jesus died to not only
forgive our sin - but also to break its power over us. He can remove those
chains that bind us. He can change us from the inside out. No one has to
stay stuck in dysfunctional lifestyles.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">May we pray the prayer
of King David in Psalm 51:10. &quot;Create in me a clean heart, oh God, and
renew a right spirit within me.&quot;</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Our &quot;empty
ways&quot; have done enough damage. Continuing on in our mistakes will get
us nothing but more pain. God is ready to transform our hearts, minds, and
lives so we can enjoy the abundant life that Jesus came to give. With His
transforming power in our lives, we can declare, &quot;Dysfunctional
behavior stops in this generation!&quot;</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><br />
<br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><br />
<br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Additional Thought to
Ponder:&nbsp; Just because you had a lousy childhood is no excuse to become
a lousy adult.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><a name="OLE_LINK2"></a><a
name="OLE_LINK1"></a><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">.....</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">Marsha Jordan (</font></font><font color="#0000ff"><a
href="mailto:jordans@newnorth.net"><font color="#000000"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><span style="TEXT-DECORATION:
